<br />
As of March 2025, Henrik Larsson is the all-time joint fourteenth top goalscorer in European club football competitions with a total of 59 goals from his time at [[Feyenoord]], Celtic, [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]], [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] and [[Helsingborgs IF]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Who has scored 50+ UEFA club goals?|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0257-0e91daaa4ec8-19686ad1d08f-1000--uefa-club-competition-all-time-top-scorers-cristiano-ron/|publisher=UEFA|access-date=11 January 2020|date=11 January 2020}}</ref>

Tommy Gemmell was the first British player to score in two different European Cup finals, scoring in 1967 against [[Inter Milan]] and then in 1970 against Feyenoord.<ref>{{cite web|last=Murray|first=Scott|title=Knowledge unlimited|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2000/jul/19/newsstory.sport4|website=The Guardian|access-date=10 July 2015|date=19 July 2000}}</ref>

In November 2012, Georgios Samaras became the first Celtic player to score in five consecutive away matches in European club competition.<ref>{{cite web|last=Burns|first=Scott|title=Benfica 2 - Celtic 1: Celtic now need a favour|url=http://www.express.co.uk/sport/football/359541/Benfica-2-Celtic-1-Celtic-now-need-a-favour|website=Daily Express|access-date=10 July 2015|date=21 November 2012}}</ref>

