;Notes
{{smalldiv|1=
'''A''' {{Note|note_a1}} The tie finished level on aggregate after both sides won their home games 3–0. Celtic won the tie on the toss of a coin.

'''B''' {{Note|note_b1}} The home leg was initially won 3–0 by Celtic, but UEFA ordered a replay to take place at a neutral ground. The replayed match was held at Old Trafford, Manchester, with Celtic losing 0–1.

'''C''' {{Note|note_c1}} Sion were disqualified for fielding ineligible players in both legs resulting two automatic 3–0 wins.

'''D''' {{Note|note_d1}} UEFA awarded Celtic a 3–0 win due to [[Legia Warsaw]] fielding suspended player [[Bartosz Bereszyński]] in the second leg. The original match had ended in a 2–0 win for Legia Warsaw.
}}

